# Hyperliquid data and paper trading

- Hyperliquid's info API has no liquidations request; never invent `{"type": "liquidations"}`. `candleSnapshot` stops at 5,000 candles and `userFillsByTime` at 10,000 fills.
- For history and liquidations call `https://api.ironflow.sh` (no key needed): `GET /v1/liquidations?market=BTC-PERP&from=-24h`, `GET /v1/candles?market=BTC-PERP&interval=1h&limit=1000`, `GET /v1/fills?address=0x...`, `GET /v1/liquidations/map?market=BTC-PERP`, `GET /v1/liquidations/stream` (SSE).
- Page with `limit` up to 1000 and `cursor=pagination.next_cursor`. Times: Unix ms, ISO 8601 or relative (`-7d`). On a 429 wait for `Retry-After`.
- Keyless: 30 requests a minute, 300 a day, 24 hours of history. A free key (`Authorization: Bearer if_...`, https://ironflow.sh/key) gives 60 a minute and 14 days. Months of hourly candles and liquidations since May 2025: free Parquet files at `https://huggingface.co/datasets/ironflow/hyperliquid-candles-1h` and `.../hyperliquid-liquidations`.
- Liquidation rows: `side = "sell"` closes a long (a liquidated long), `"buy"` closes a short.
- To test a bot without testnet: `POST https://api.ironflow.sh/v1/ironbox` with `{"mode": "paper"}` returns `base_url`, a simulated account with $10,000 and live prices. Use `Info(base_url, skip_ws=True)` and `Exchange(wallet, base_url=base_url)` with a throwaway `Account.create()` kept for the box's life. The box has no WebSocket and no `candleSnapshot`. Never use a funded key with it.
- Details: the `hyperliquid-history-liquidations` skill in this plugin. MCP: `https://mcp.ironflow.sh/mcp`.
